bc7enc_rdo ert: hash_hsieh without misaligned loads or a left shift of a negative value

ert::hash_hsieh() hashes byte runs at any offset inside the block array (the match search of
the rate-distortion pass). It read them as `*reinterpret_cast<const uint16_t*>(p)`, which is a
misaligned load (undefined behaviour) for odd offsets, and shifted a negative `signed char`
left by 18, which is undefined too. UBSan (Clang, -fsanitize=undefined) stops at ert.cpp:238
"load of misaligned address" and ert.cpp:263 "left shift of negative value" on the texture
importer's RDO tests (DENG-99).

The loads now go through memcpy into a uint16_t, and the sign-extended byte is converted to
uint32_t before the shift. Both give the same bits as before on every two's-complement host,
so hash values and the encoder's output do not change.

Engine-local patch (DENG-99), applied by tools/vendor/vendor.py. Drop it when a pinned commit
has the fix.

diff --git a/ert.cpp b/ert.cpp
index 4a37f95..aaa51cf 100644
--- a/ert.cpp
+++ b/ert.cpp
@@ -233,7 +233,8 @@ namespace ert
 
 		while (len--)
 		{
-			const uint16_t* pWords = reinterpret_cast<const uint16_t*>(pBuf);
+			uint16_t pWords[2];
+			memcpy(pWords, pBuf, sizeof(pWords));
 
 			h += pWords[0];
 
@@ -253,16 +254,24 @@ namespace ert
 			h += h >> 1;
 			break;
 		case 2:
-			h += *reinterpret_cast<const uint16_t*>(pBuf);
+		{
+			uint16_t w;
+			memcpy(&w, pBuf, sizeof(w));
+			h += w;
 			h ^= h << 11;
 			h += h >> 17;
 			break;
+		}
 		case 3:
-			h += *reinterpret_cast<const uint16_t*>(pBuf);
+		{
+			uint16_t w;
+			memcpy(&w, pBuf, sizeof(w));
+			h += w;
 			h ^= h << 16;
-			h ^= (static_cast<signed char>(pBuf[sizeof(uint16_t)])) << 18;
+			h ^= static_cast<uint32_t>(static_cast<int32_t>(static_cast<signed char>(pBuf[sizeof(uint16_t)]))) << 18;
 			h += h >> 11;
 			break;
+		}
 		default:
 			break;
 		}
